{"path":"language/do","title":"do-while loop","titleHtml":"<code>do</code>-<code>while</code> loop","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/do","section":"language","kind":"page","summary":"Conditionally executes a statement repeatedly (at least once).","html":"<p>Conditionally executes a statement repeatedly (at least once).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Syntax\">Syntax</h3>\n<table class=\"t-sdsc-begin\">\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"10\" class=\"t-sdsc-sep\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-sdsc\">\n<td class=\"t-sdsc-nopad\"> <span class=\"t-spar\">attr</span> ﻿<span class=\"t-mark\">(optional)</span> <code><b>do</b></code> <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span> <code><b>while (</b></code> <span class=\"t-spar\">expression</span> <code><b>);</b></code>\n</td>\n<td class=\"t-sdsc-nopad\">\n</td>\n<td class=\"t-sdsc-nopad\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"10\" class=\"t-sdsc-sep\">\n</td></tr></table>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> <span class=\"t-spar\">attr</span>\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> any number of <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/attributes\">attributes</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> <span class=\"t-spar\">expression</span>\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> an <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/expressions\">expression</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span>\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/statements\">statement</a> (typically a compound statement)\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Explanation\">Explanation</h3>\n<p>When control reaches a <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">do</span></span> statement, its <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span> will be executed unconditionally.\n</p><p>Every time <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span> finishes its execution, <span class=\"t-spar\">expression</span> will be evaluated and contextually converted to <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">bool</span></span>. If the result is <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>, <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span> will be executed again.\n</p><p>If the loop needs to be terminated within <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span>, a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/break\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">break</span></span> statement</a> can be used as terminating statement.\n</p><p>If the current iteration needs to be terminated within <span class=\"t-spar\">statement</span>, a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/continue\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">continue</span></span> statement</a> can be used as shortcut.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>As part of the C++ <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/multithread#Progress_guarantee\">forward progress guarantee</a>, the behavior is <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/ub\">undefined</a> if a loop<span class=\"t-rev-inl t-since-cxx26\"><span> that is not a <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/multithread#Trivial_infinite_loops\">trivial infinite loop</a></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(since C++26)</span></span></span> without <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/as_if\">observable behavior</a> does not terminate. Compilers are permitted to remove such loops.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Keywords\">Keywords</h3>\n<p><a href=\"/w/cpp/keyword/do\"><code>do</code></a>,\n<a href=\"/w/cpp/keyword/while\"><code>while</code></a>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> j <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">do</span> <span class=\"co1\">// compound statement is the loop body</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        j <span class=\"sy2\">+</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> j <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span>j <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// common situation where do-while loop is used</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a> s <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"aba\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/sort\"><span class=\"kw1630\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sort</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, s.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">do</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> s <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// expression statement is the loop body</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">while</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/next_permutation\"><span class=\"kw1661\">std::<span class=\"me2\">next_permutation</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, s.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>4 6 8 10\naab\naba\nbaa</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/language/do\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>do-while</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Syntax","id":"Syntax"},{"depth":3,"text":"Explanation","id":"Explanation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Keywords","id":"Keywords"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"language","title":"C++ language"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"do-while loop","children":[{"label":"Syntax","note":"attr, expression, statement"},{"label":"Explanation","note":"When control reaches a do statement, its statement will be executed unconditionally."},{"label":"Notes","note":"As part of the C++ forward progress guarantee, the behavior is undefined if a loop that is not a trivial infinite loop(since C++26) without observable…"},{"label":"Keywords","note":"do, while"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":["C++11","C++26"],"wordCount":236,"codeBlockCount":2}
